  "title": "# Lander A — make finished builds landable For each build below, in order, work in its folder /root…",
  "asked": "# Lander A — make finished builds landable For each build below, in order, work in its folder /root/axf-builds/<name> (if missing, try /home/axfbuild/wt-<name>; if still missing, log it and skip): 1. `git checkout -- _claude/builds/` and `git clean -fd _claude/builds/` (those are auto-synced data, never real work). Keep any other uncommitted change: commit it as `<name>: commit leftover work`. 2. `git fetch origin && git merge origin/main`. Resolve clashes keeping BOTH sides' intent; for _claude/builds/** JSON take main's version. 3. Run the tests/checks for the touched area (and `node framework/spec/check-*.mjs` that relate). Fix what this branch broke. 4. Commit. Do NOT push. 5. If it can't be made green in ~30 min, `git merge --abort`/reset to the branch's last commit and log it as SKIPPED with the reason. Progress: at the start and end of every build append one line to /root/axf-builds/lander-a/PROGRESS.md: `<time> <name> START` / `<time> <name> READY|SKIPPED <reason>`. Don't stop between builds. Builds: dataset-bar, icon-browser-manager, library-harvest, lib-moremenu, merge-conflict-alerts, ui-asset-designer, approvals-in-place-r2, settings-sections-everywhere Don't touch other folders. Don't start other builds. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
